---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { registry, quotes } from '../lib/quote-data';
import { collections } from '../lib/collections';
import { tricksters } from '../lib/tricksters';
import { resources, videos } from '../lib/resource-catalog';
const withReferences = quotes.filter((quote) => Boolean(quote.reference)).length;
const authors = new Set(quotes.map((quote) => quote.person)).size;
---
<BaseLayout title="Sources & Attribution — Jester Quotes" description="Learn where Jester Quotes' original 100 quotations came from, how author references are preserved, and how to report a correction.">
  <div class="wrap discovery-page">
    <header class="discovery-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Behind the curtain / Provenance</p>
      <h1>Credit where it's <em>due.</em></h1>
      <p class="lede">A collection can celebrate the fool and still be serious about attribution. Here is what the registry actually documents—and what it does not.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="sources-grid">
      <section class="source-panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">01 / Collection source</p>
        <h2>One supplied collection.</h2>
        <p>The 100-quotation registry derives from <a href={registry.source.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{registry.source.name}</a>. The original source link is provided across the site.</p>
        <p>Author names and available reference fields are preserved as provided; they have not been independently verified for every quotation.</p>
        <a class="btn secondary" href={registry.source.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View source article ↗</a>
      </section>
      <section class="source-panel source-panel--numbers">
        <p class="eyebrow">02 / Registry at a glance</p>
        <div class="source-stats">
          <div><strong>{quotes.length}</strong><span>quoted entries</span></div>
          <div><strong>{authors}</strong><span>attributed names</span></div>
          <div><strong>{withReferences}</strong><span>with source references</span></div>
        </div>
        <p>{quotes.length - withReferences} entries have no additional reference field in the supplied dataset. Missing citations are not invented.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="source-panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">03 / Editorial organization</p>
        <h2>Themes, not new attributions.</h2>
        <p>The {collections.length} themed collections are editorial groupings created for discovery. A quotation may appear in more than one theme; those labels are not original source metadata and do not establish what an author intended.</p>
        <a class="section-text-link" href="/collections/">Explore the themes ↗</a>
      </section>
      <section class="source-panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">04 / Reuse & correction</p>
        <h2>Attribution isn't a license.</h2>
        <p>Credit to an author or source does not establish permission to reproduce third-party text. Republishing, printing, merchandising, or wider redistribution may require rights clearance or another valid legal basis.</p>
        <p>Found a misattribution or correction? <a href="https://github.com/JFeimster/jester-quotes/issues/new" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Submit an issue on GitHub</a> with the quotation number and supporting source. No corrections are automatically applied to the original registry.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="source-panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">05 / Trickster directory</p>
        <h2>Independent reference notes.</h2>
        <p>The <a href="/tricksters/">Trickster Directory</a> contains {tricksters.length} short original profiles backed by external references. It is a curated introduction, not a reproduction of another researcher's list or a claim that every culture interprets these figures alike.</p>
        <p><a href="https://www.aadip.com/trickster/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Aadip Desai’s Trickster Hit List!</a> contains 139 numbered research leads and is credited as inspiration, not reproduced. A separate unpublished research-candidate CSV is maintained. No third-party character pictures were copied.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="source-panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">06 / Linked resources and video catalog</p>
        <h2>Original sources stay original.</h2>
        <p>The <a href="/resources/">Resource Vault</a> has {resources.length} independently linked references and the <a href="/videos/">Video Library</a> features {videos.length} verified YouTube links. All summaries are written for this site, and the original publishers retain their content.</p>
        <p>Resource cards link outward to their original pages. Video embeds are not loaded until a visitor chooses to load the YouTube player; external video links work without embedding. Publisher inclusion does not imply endorsement or grant any media reuse permission.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
    <p class="curation-note">Original quotation records remain in <a href="https://github.com/JFeimster/jester-quotes/blob/main/src/data/jester-quotes.json" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the public source registry</a>. The corresponding credit policy is in <a href="https://github.com/JFeimster/jester-quotes/blob/main/CREDITS.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CREDITS.md</a>.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
